            <description><![CDATA[<h2>RestinPID 3.3</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Totals at a glance:</b> each group heading shows its total RAM and CPU. Or choose <i>Whole Mac</i> to see memory used and CPU load as Activity Monitor shows them. Settings → Usage.</li>
<li><b>Menu bar reading:</b> optionally show RAM and CPU next to the menu bar icon, either for the apps in the list or for the whole Mac. Settings → Usage.</li>
<li><b>Hide quiet apps:</b> show only busy apps. You decide what busy means: over your RAM limit <b>or</b> your CPU limit, or over <b>both</b> at once. Settings → Apps.</li>
<li><b>Restart RestinPID</b> with the new button next to the gear.</li>
<li><b>Tidier Settings:</b> new Apps and Usage tabs, and self-restart has moved to Auto-Restart.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
